Reverse phase-encoding susceptibility distortion correction for the sdc web app
and its command line.

The WebAssembly module src/sdc.wasm is built from the Rust crates
exes/sdc/core and exes/sdc/wasm by scripts/build-wasm.sh. exes/sdc/core/src/hysco.rs ports PyHySCO 0.0.4 (https://github.com/EmoryMLIP/PyHySCO,
PyPI release 0.0.4; its git commit bff6655 differs only in the name of the
initialization class), Copyright (c) Abigail Julian and Lars Ruthotto, under
the GNU General Public License version 3 (LICENSE). This workspace is
distributed under the GNU General Public License, version 3 or (at your
option) any later version.

Julian A, Ruthotto L (2024). PyHySCO: GPU-enabled susceptibility artifact
distortion correction in seconds. arXiv:2403.10706.

Ruthotto L, Kugel H, Olesch J, Fischer B, Modersitzki J, Burger M, Wolters CH
(2012). Diffeomorphic susceptibility artifact correction of diffusion-weighted
magnetic resonance images. Phys Med Biol 57(18):5715-5731.

The separate ./field-fit entry point and sdc-field-fit.wasm contain the deterministic
sdcflows 2.17.1 field conversion and B-spline fit, Apache-2.0, with a portable
OpenBLAS SkylakeX dot reduction, BSD-3-Clause. These files do not contain the
PyHySCO implementation. See LICENSE-SDCFLOW and LICENSE-OPENBLAS. Existing
PyHySCO files retain their GPL-3.0-or-later notices and licensing.

